WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:06.490
This pretty and useful braid is
easy to knit on the machine.

2
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.100
Use tuck stitch for texture
over a few stitches.

3
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:17.760
Cast on an odd number of stitches
and knit a few rows and hang some weight.

4
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.580
Set your carriage to hold.

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.280
If you're not familiar with the hold

6
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.480
setting on your machine, check your
manual and watch the video at knititnow.

7
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.700
Com/HOLD.

8
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.760
Pull the center needle all the way out.

9
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:38.020
Knit four to 6 rows,
holding that center needle.

10
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.700
Notice how loops are formed
over the held needle.

11
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:50.720
Cancel hold and knit two rows.

12
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.480
Continue this sequence for the
desired length of your braid.

13
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.400
Depending on your machine and your chosen

14
00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:10.800
yarn, you are limited to the
number of rows you can hold.

15
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.770
Those loops stack up and may
be difficult to knit.

16
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.900
You may need to add extra weight with your

17
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.420
fingers or claw weights so
the stitches knit off correctly.

18
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.850
Try different row counts
and see what works for you.

19
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.930
Here is a pretty variation.

20
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:36.180
In this example, I cast on nine needles
and held two stitches for six rows.

21
00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:40.570
This makes a wider braid
with a pretty scalloped edge.

22
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.560
Both sides are interesting.

23
00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.180
Here's a five stitch braid
on a standard gauge machine.

24
00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.160
Holding with the Russell levers

25
00:01:55.190 --> 00:02:02.440
on a Silver Reed machine creates manual
tuck stitch for the texture of this

26
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.320
braid. No

27
00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.400
matter what machine you use,

28
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.400
I hope you'll play with the technique
to create a fancy braid of your own.

